https://github.com/GoogleContainerTools/jib/tree/master/jib-maven-plugin

1. Add the Jib plugin to your pom.xml
2. Configure the Jib plugin to specify the base image and target image:
```xml
<build>
  <plugins>
    <plugin>
      <groupId>com.google.cloud.tools</groupId>
      <artifactId>jib-maven-plugin</artifactId>
      <version>3.1.4</version>
      <configuration>
        <from>
          <image>openjdk:17-jdk-slim</image>
        </from>
        <to>
          <image>your-dockerhub-username/your-image-name:tag</image>
        </to>
      </configuration>
    </plugin>
  </plugins>
</build>
```
3. Build the Docker image using the Jib plugin:
```bash mvn compile jib:build
```
This command will compile your application and build the Docker image, pushing it to the specified registry.
4. Run the Docker image:
```bash docker run -p 9000:9000 your-dockerhub-username/your-image-name:tag
```This command will run the Docker container and map port 8080 of the container to port 9000 on your host machine, allowing you to access the application at http://localhost:9000.